nodes.statement:
We will prove the following claim: there exists $N\ge1$ such that, for any $I \in 
uzh$, the inclusion map $i_N:NI	o I$ induces the zero map $0=(i_N)_*: F_0(NI) 	o F_0(I)$. Once this is done, the statement of the lemma will follow by applying (1) and (3) to the short exact sequence $NI	o I	o I/NI$. As in Corollary~ef{rationalhens}, let $[N]: \mathbb{Z}\left\{x_1, \dots, x_night\}^+ 	o \mathbb{Z}\left\{x_1, \dots, x_night\}^+$ be the operator that multiplies each $x_i$ by $N$, so that the colimit of the $[N]$, indexed over $N\ge1$ ordered by divisibility, is $\mathbb{Q}\left\{x_1, \dots, x_night\}^+$. By assumption $F_0$ commutes with filtered colimits and annihilates any nonunital henselian $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra; so, given any element $u \in F_0(\mathbb{Z}\left\{x_1, \dots, x_night\}^+)$, it follows that there exists $N > 0$ such that $[N]_*(u) = 0$. Now we use that $F_0$ is projectively finitely generated. This means that there exists a surjection \[  igoplus_{i=1}^t \mathbb{Z}[\mathrm{Hom}_{
uzh}(\mathbb{Z}\left\{x_1, \dots, x_{n_i}ight\}^+, \cdot)] 	o F_0\] of functors for some $n_1,\dots,n_t\ge1$. For each $i=1,\dots,t$, let $g_i\in F_0(\mathbb{Z}\left\{x_1, \dots, x_{n_i}ight\}^+)$ be the image of $\mathrm{id}\in \mathrm{Hom}_{
uzh}(\mathbb{Z}\left\{x_1, \dots, x_{n_i}ight\}^+, \mathbb{Z}\left\{x_1, \dots, x_{n_i}ight\}^+)$. Then the above surjection concretely means the following: given any $I\in 
uzh$ and any element $y\in F_0(I)$, then $y$ is a finite sum of elements of $F_0(I)$ obtained by pushing forward the $g_i$ along various maps $\phi:\mathbb{Z}\left\{x_1, \dots, x_{n_i}ight\}^+ 	o I$. By the second paragraph, there exists an integer $N > 0$ such that $[N]_*(g_i)=0$ for all the generators $g_i$. From this we can easily complete the proof of the claim, as follows. Given any $I \in 
uzh$, every map $\phi: \mathbb{Z}\{ x_1, \dots, x_{n_i}\}^+ 	o N I $ has the property that the composite $i_N \circ \phi: \mathbb{Z}\left\{x_1, \dots, x_{n_i}ight\}^+ 	o I$ factors through $[N]$, i.e., one has a commutative diagram in $
uzh$ \[ \xymatrix{ \mathbb{Z}\left\{x_1, \dots, x_night\}^+ \ar[r]_-{\phi}\ar[d]^{[N]} & NI \ar[d]^{i_N} \ \mathbb{Z}\left\{x_1, \dots, x_night\}^+ \ar[r] & I }.\] By choice of $N$ it follows that the composite \[ \mathbb{Z}[\mathrm{Hom}_{
uzh}( \mathbb{Z}\left\{x_1, \dots, x_{n_i}ight\}^+, NI)] 	o F_0(NI) 	o F_0(I) \] is zero. But we have shown that every element of $F_0(NI)$ is a finite sum of elements of the form $\phi_*(g_i)$ for various maps $\phi$. Since $g_i \in F_0( \mathbb{Z}\left\{x_1, \dots, x_{n_i}ight\}^+)$ is annihilated by $[N]$, it follows that $(i_N)_*: F_0(NI) 	o F_0(I)$ is zero, as claimed.

Now we use that $F_0$ is projectively finitely generated. This means that there exists a surjection \[  igoplus_{i=1}^t \mathbb{Z}[\mathrm{Hom}_{
uzh}(\mathbb{Z}\left\{x_1, \dots, x_{n_i}ight\}^+, \cdot)] 	o F_0\] of functors for some $n_1,\dots,n_t\ge1$. For each $i=1,\dots,t$, let $g_i\in F_0(\mathbb{Z}\left\{x_1, \dots, x_{n_i}ight\}^+)$ be the image of $\mathrm{id}\in \mathrm{Hom}_{
uzh}(\mathbb{Z}\left\{x_1, \dots, x_{n_i}ight\}^+, \mathbb{Z}\left\{x_1, \dots, x_{n_i}ight\}^+)$. Then the above surjection concretely means the following: given any $I\in 
uzh$ and any element $y\in F_0(I)$, then $y$ is a finite sum of elements of $F_0(I)$ obtained by pushing forward the $g_i$ along various maps $\phi:\mathbb{Z}\left\{x_1, \dots, x_{n_i}ight\}^+ 	o I$.

